WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.640
People are saying let's show
them the art of the possible.

2
00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:06.040
That always makes me chuckle a
little inside because I'm a wordcel.

3
00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:07.700
I love history,
politics, language,

4
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:10.000
and that phrase doesn't mean
what people think it means.

5
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.720
In fact, it comes from
Otto von Bismarck,

6
00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:13.660
if you can believe that.

7
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.780
Politics is the art
of the possible,

8
00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:16.440
he said.

9
00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:17.940
He meant something precise.

10
00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.540
You can dream up the
perfect world all you want,

11
00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:24.920
but power and needs and limited
resources force you to work with

12
00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:27.180
what can actually
get done, compromise,

13
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.100
constraints, and trade-offs.

14
00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:33.500
His point is you have to be realistic
about what you're going to do.

15
00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:35.460
You can never get
to the dreamland.

16
00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:38.260
So let me ask you when you say let's
show them the art of the possible.

17
00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:39.380
What are you really saying?

18
00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:42.060
You're saying I want to show
the customer every amazing thing

19
00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:45.400
our software does in a dreamland
where they've implemented every

20
00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:47.320
single thing we sell.

21
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:49.920
It's the fifth generation version
of everything the platform

22
00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:51.400
could do someday.

23
00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:52.420
And here's the thing.

24
00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:54.940
Most of your own customers,
they never get there.

25
00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:57.500
Not even the ones that have
been there with you for years.

26
00:00:57.780 --> 00:00:59.080
Certainly not the new ones.

27
00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:01.180
So you're not showing
them the possible.

28
00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:04.280
You're showing them the impossible
and empty promise dressed up

29
00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:07.320
as insights to sell your widgets.

30
00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:11.020
So I want you to stop saying let's
show them the art of the possible.

31
00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:15.000
You should be saying software
is the art of the possible too.

32
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.880
Next time you run a demo, ask
yourself what you're really showing.

33
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:22.480
The five-year fantasy they'll
never reach or specific achievable

34
00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:26.680
things they can do in the next 90
days to make their lives better.

35
00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:28.320
Show them the possible.
